- op: discuss  # ebe8
  at: '2026-06-02T17:34:25Z'  # ebe8
  by: agent  # ebe8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ebe8
  clock: 6  # ebe8
  nonce: ebe8  # ebe8
  message: "Pass-35 F35.D2 — `search --limit` accepts more invalid-numeric-sentinel values silently than just negative integers.\n\nINV-toniv's existing scope: \"Negative --limit values accepted silently (Python slice abuse)\". Pass-35 D.3 probe enumerated 5 --limit values:\n\n```\n--limit -1         : rc=0  header=545  (returns all post-filter; per existing scope)\n--limit 0          : rc=0  header=545  (interpreted as no-limit, NOT as \"show 0\")\n--limit 1          : rc=0  header=1    (sensible — minimal positive case works)\n--limit abc        : rc=2  argparse rejects cleanly (non-numeric correctly errors)\n--limit 99999999999: rc=0  header=545  (numeric overflow silently accepted as no-limit)\n```\n\nThree sentinel-like values (0 / -1 / overflow) all produce \"no limit\" behavior:\n- `--limit 0` returns all 545 matches, not 0 — the natural reading of \"limit=0\" → \"no results\" is contradicted\n- `--limit -1` produces tail-drop slicing per existing INV-toniv scope (header=545 here because the slice still produces ≥1 record on this 571-match query)\n- `--limit 99999999999` (Python int parses fine; no upper bound check) accepted as no-limit equivalent\n\n`--help` text says \"Maximum number of results to show (default: 20)\" — does NOT document:\n- limit=0 sentinel semantics (no-limit vs zero-results)\n- limit upper bound or overflow handling\n- negative limit behavior (per existing INV-toniv title)\n\nThree silent-accept cases, three different \"no limit\" behaviors. The argparse type=int catches non-numeric like `abc`, but type-validation on numeric doesn't establish a useful range. Same INV-toniv title scope applies — pass-35 widens the symptom catalog.\n\n**Fix-path candidate.** Apply `argparse type=` factory function with range-check: positive integers only, with explicit \"0 means no limit\" documented or rejected. Sibling pattern to other --limit-style flags across hypergumbo subcommands; could be a shared `positive_int` / `limit_int` argparse type factory.\n\n**Probe artifact:** `/tmp/p35_outputD.log` D.3 (5 --limit values tested). No status change."  # ebe8
